# CHAPTER II

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

#### Article 4

Women and children who are victims of acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity shall receive the following rights:  
a. Right to guarantee space for community participation in government, including in decision-making/policy-making;  
b. Right to population documents and civil registration;  
c. Right to Legal Aid;  
d. Right to be respected for their dignity and worth as human beings;  
e. Right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;  
f. Right to determine their own decisions;  
g. Right to obtain information;  
h. Right to confidentiality;  
i. Right to compensation;  
j. Right to social rehabilitation;  
k. Right to complaint handling;  
l. Right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and  
m. Right to assistance.

#### Article 5

Child victims of acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, shall also receive special rights, as follows:  
a. Right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;  
b. Right to basic services;  
c. Right to equal protection;  
d. Right to be free from various stigma;  
e. Right to employment;  
f. Right to decent housing and environment;  
g. Right to Women's empowerment; and  
h. Right to prevention of violence.

# CHAPTER III

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

#### Article 6

Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children are the shared responsibility of:  
a. regional government;  
b. community;  
c. family;  
d. parents; and  
e. non-governmental institutions including Customary Institutions and Business Entities.

#### Article 7

The obligations and responsibilities of regional government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:  
a. implementing protection policies for women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity as determined by the government;  
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity;  
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity;  
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity;  
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity for women and children according to regional financial capacity; and  
f. fostering and supervising the implementation and protection of women and children from acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity.

#### Article 8

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 6 letter b shall be implemented in the form of community participation. (2) The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:  
a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity against women and children;  
b. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties; and  
c. participating in providing assistance and/or handling of victims of acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades their dignity and humanity against women and children.  
2. The form of participation shall be carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 9

The obligations of family and/or parents as referred to in Article 6 letter c and letter d, who legally have full responsibility to prevent all forms of violence and protect women and children as family members.

